# Copy to secrets.env and fill in.
#
# SECURITY — never commit secrets.env or a filled configs/jellyflam3.yaml.
# Both are gitignored. If git ever tracks them again:
#   git rm --cached secrets.env configs/jellyflam3.yaml
#   rotate the Jellyfin API key immediately
# Host-local only: each Pi has its own API key / user / library IDs.
# Do not scp secrets between Pis; do not restore secrets from shared git history.

# On-box API (worker, smoke probes). Often loopback on the Pi.
JELLYFIN_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8096
JELLYFIN_API_KEY=
JELLYFIN_USER_ID=
JELLYFIN_LIBRARY_ID=

# Optional: client-facing base for VLC_URL in scripts/hls_smoke.sh.
# If unset, the script auto-detects LAN IP from the default route.
# JELLYFIN_PUBLIC_URL=http://192.168.x.x:8096
# JELLYFIN_LAN_HOST=192.168.x.x

# Optional power-user credential for furnace-built sideload clients. Unique per
# furnace — do not copy from another Pi. Store Roku and ordinary Kodi installs
# authenticate votes and Fetch TV display with JELLYFIN_API_KEY instead.
# The sink exits 2 (crash-loop) only when both this token and JELLYFIN_API_KEY
# are empty on a non-loopback bind.
#
# When: only if a developer/operator sideload should send this token instead of
# the Jellyfin API key. Not required for a Channel Store install.
# Where: this file on THIS Pi (`/opt/jellyflam3-server/secrets.env`).
# How (print once; paste below). Packaging on this Pi copies it into the private
# Roku preset and the Kodi display_sink_token default. There is no Roku Settings row.
#   python3 -c 'import secrets; print(secrets.token_urlsafe(32))'
#
# Header X-JellyFlam3-Token. Loopback-only binds may omit both secrets;
# --allow-unauthenticated is lab-only and is not in the unit file.
#
# Limitation: JELLYFIN_API_KEY then also authorizes vote and display-profile
# writes. Reconsider if those should be a separate credential again.
DISPLAY_SINK_TOKEN=

# Tailscale pre-auth key for flock peering Opt In (Phase 2 guide 05). Never commit.
# Create a tagged key (tag:jellyflam3) in the Tailscale admin console.
# TS_AUTHKEY=tskey-auth-...
